of human experiments</article-title><source>Daedalus</source><year>1969</year><fpage>523</fpage><lpage>541</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chalmers</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The impact of controlled trials on the practice of medicine</article-title><source>Mt Sinai J Med</source><year>1974</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>753</fpage><lpage>759</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4547818</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Prescott</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Counsell</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillespie</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Grant</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>IT</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiauka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Colthart</surname><given-names>IR</given-names></name><name><surname>Ross</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Shepherd</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Factors that limit the quality, number and progress of randomised controlled trials</article-title><source>Health Technol Assess</source><year>1999</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>143</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10683591</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schulz</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name><name><surname>Chalmers</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayes</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Altman</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name></person-group><article-ti